From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] compasschain: link the sibling libraries it calls into

CompassChain::resetCalibration() forwards to MagCalibrationChain, but the
plugin only added magcalibrationchain to INCLUDEPATH and never linked it. The
library builds regardless, carrying an undefined
_ZN19MagCalibrationChain16resetCalibrationEv with no DT_NEEDED that could
resolve it, and sensorfwd then rejects it at load:

  Plugin loading error: "compasschain" - "Cannot load library
  /usr/lib/sensord-qt6/libcompasschain-qt6.so: undefined symbol:
  _ZN19MagCalibrationChain16resetCalibrationEv"
  plugin marked invalid: "compasschain" / "compasssensor"

compasssensor is invalidated along with it, and sensortestapp aborts outright
with the shipped testapp.conf because loading that plugin fails.

This is not a one-off. Resolving each undefined symbol only exposes the next,
because none of the siblings on INCLUDEPATH were ever linked:

  undefined symbol: _ZN19MagCalibrationChain16resetCalibrationEv
  undefined symbol: _ZN16DownsampleFilter10setTimeoutEi
  undefined symbol: _ZN17DeclinationFilter21declinationCorrectionEv

so all of them are linked here rather than chasing them one at a time. The
original instance was: CompassChain also casts
downsampleFilter to DownsampleFilter and calls setTimeout() on it, while
downsamplefilter was likewise only on INCLUDEPATH. With just the
magcalibrationchain link in place the loader simply reaches the next one:

  Cannot load library /usr/lib/sensord-qt6/libcompasschain-qt6.so:
  undefined symbol: _ZN16DownsampleFilter10setTimeoutEi

so both have to be linked. rotationsensor is invalidated along with
compasschain, which is why QtSensors clients (Messwerk) saw no rotation while
the UI - which reads orientation/accelerometer - still rotated.

Link them the same way every other component here links a sibling library, and
declare the build dependency that link implies. chains/ is not CONFIG+=ordered
- only the top-level .pro is, and that only serialises chains against filters,
sensors, ... not the subdirs inside chains/ - so without compasschain.depends
make starts both subdirs at once and the link races the library it needs:

  ld: cannot find -lmagcalibrationchain-qt6

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/chains/compasschain/compasschain.pro
+++ b/chains/compasschain/compasschain.pro
@@ -17,4 +17,25 @@
                ../../filters/magcoordinatealignfilter \
                ../../filters/declinationfilter
 
+# CompassChain calls into every one of the siblings above, but the plugin only
+# ever put them on INCLUDEPATH and never linked any of them. The .so builds
+# regardless, carrying undefined symbols with no DT_NEEDED that could resolve
+# them, and sensorfwd rejects it at load - one symbol at a time, so fixing them
+# individually just moves the error:
+#   undefined symbol: _ZN19MagCalibrationChain16resetCalibrationEv
+#   undefined symbol: _ZN16DownsampleFilter10setTimeoutEi
+#   undefined symbol: _ZN17DeclinationFilter21declinationCorrectionEv
+# compasssensor and rotationsensor are invalidated along with compasschain, and
+# rotationsensor is what QtSensors clients (Messwerk) ask for - which is why
+# rotation never reported while the UI, reading orientation/accelerometer, still
+# rotated. sensortestapp also aborts with the stock testapp.conf.
+#
+# Link the lot, so this cannot regress one symbol at a time again.
+LIBS += -L../magcalibrationchain            -lmagcalibrationchain-qt$${QT_MAJOR_VERSION}
+LIBS += -L../../filters/downsamplefilter    -ldownsamplefilter-qt$${QT_MAJOR_VERSION}
+LIBS += -L../../filters/declinationfilter   -ldeclinationfilter-qt$${QT_MAJOR_VERSION}
+LIBS += -L../../filters/coordinatealignfilter -lcoordinatealignfilter-qt$${QT_MAJOR_VERSION}
+LIBS += -L../../filters/magcoordinatealignfilter -lmagcoordinatealignfilter-qt$${QT_MAJOR_VERSION}
+LIBS += -L../../filters/avgaccfilter        -lavgaccfilter-qt$${QT_MAJOR_VERSION}
+
 include( ../chain-config.pri )
--- a/chains/chains.pro	2026-09-03 10:01:13.366234061 +0200
+++ b/chains/chains.pro	2026-09-03 10:01:13.372234167 +0200
@@ -7,3 +7,12 @@
            orientationchain \
            magcalibrationchain \
            compasschain
+
+# compasschain links -lmagcalibrationchain-qt$${QT_MAJOR_VERSION}, so it cannot
+# be built at the same time as the chain it links. This directory is not
+# CONFIG+=ordered (only the top level is, and that only serialises chains
+# against filters, sensors, ... - not the subdirs within it), so without an
+# explicit dependency make is free to start both at once and compasschain's
+# link step loses the race:
+#   ld: cannot find -lmagcalibrationchain-qt6
+compasschain.depends = magcalibrationchain
